  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "AI infrastructure backlog carries FY2027 to +6%, then ~4% long-run growth from IT spend above GDP, share gains and tuck-in services M&A; EBITDA-pre-SBC margin rebuilds only to 8.8% (from 8.6% FY2026E, vs 9.5% FY2023-24) as services offset lower-margin AI hardware mix.",
    "bull": "AI capex is a multi-year enterprise build plus a PC refresh: +11% FY2027, >5% growth into FY2031; services (Mission Cloud, Lovelytics) scale and margin returns to ~9.3%; continued share consolidation from smaller VARs.",
    "bear": "FY2026 was a pull-forward: a FY2023-style digestion (-4% FY2027, flat FY2028), OEM-direct and hyperscaler-marketplace disintermediation keep margin at 8.1%, public-sector budget and DOJ E-Rate risk weigh on the government/education book."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "CDW is a capital-light, high-ROIC distributor whose value rests on a thin but durable ~8.5-9% EBITDA margin on a large, slowly-growing revenue base. The valuation is driven by margin (each 0.1pp of EBITDA margin is ~$25M of EBITDA) and by whether the 2026 AI hardware surge is durable or a pull-forward. Owner FCF charges SBC and award-withholding taxes (~0.5% of revenue, small) and a negative working-capital capture, since a distributor's growth consumes receivables and inventory.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "AI server/storage pull-forward reverses (FY2022->FY2023 precedent: -10% revenue)",
      "Gross margin mix compression persists below 21% as hardware-heavy AI projects dominate",
      "OEM-direct and hyperscaler-marketplace disintermediation of transactional resale",
      "Leverage up to $7.1bn gross debt after Lovelytics and new notes at 5.7-6.35% coupons",
      "Lengthening DSO (100 days) and inventory build consuming cash beyond the modelled capture",
      "Open DOJ False Claims Act inquiry into E-Rate bidding (education/public book)"
    ]
  },
