    "nci_treatment": "None; wholly-owned subsidiaries.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (dcf-methods routing row 'operating company'). CDW is a US IT value-added reseller/integrator -- an operating company with FCF; no bank, REIT or holdco features, no prior valuation or memory entry. FY0 CHOICE: FY0 is FY2026E, not FY2025, because the balance sheet anchor is 2026-09-30: projecting FY2026 as year 1 from a Sep-2026 net-debt figure would count nine months of FY2026 cash flow twice. FY2026E revenue $25,250M = 9M actual $19,006.5M + Q4 estimate ~$6,240M (Q4-2025 $5,510.6M +13%, consistent with 9M growth of +12.4% and management's 'orders outpacing invoicing, backlog building' at Q3). FY2026E EBITDA pre-SBC ~8.6% = GAAP operating income ~$1,764M (9M $1,294.1M + Q4 ~$470M) + D&A ~$305M + SBC ~$104M. GAAP operating income (not non-GAAP) is used so recurring transformation/integration costs stay in; acquisition intangible amortization stays in D&A (non-cash, added back). Historic EBITDA-pre-SBC margin: FY2022 8.9%, FY2023 9.6%, FY2024 9.5%, FY2025 9.1%, FY2026E 8.6% (AI server/storage mix compressed gross margin to 20.5% in Q3-2026 from 21.9%). Working capital: distributor with receivables + inventory > payables, so wc_capture is NEGATIVE (growth consumes cash); net working capital ~8-9% of revenue, DSO lengthening (100 days vs 92). Year-1 component check: base FY2027 owner FCF ~$1.46bn (5.4% of revenue) vs FY2025 unlevered owner FCF ~$1.24bn (reported FCF $1,088M + after-tax interest ~$176M - award taxes $26M) on $22.4bn revenue (5.5%), so no one-off is carried forward. TTM-to-Q3-2026 reported FCF is only ~$934M because inventory (AI project build, product financing arrangement) and receivables rose; treated as timing, partly captured by the negative wc_capture. Inventory financing payable ($599M) treated as trade working capital, not debt, matching CDW's own definition of net debt. The $1,009M 2.670% notes due Dec-2026 will be repaid from the cash already held, so net debt is unaffected. Interest income is not stripped: CDW is net-debt.",
